/target
node_modules/
/vendor/libghostty-vt/zig-pkg/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store

/docs/*
!/docs/next/
!/docs/next/**
!/docs/preview/
!/docs/preview/**
!/docs/versions/
!/docs/versions/**
# Fork-owned catalogues. These are cited as authoritative by this repo's own
# agent routing, so losing them breaks the workflow rather than just the docs.
# They were kept alive by `git add -f` until now, which meant every file added
# later silently fell back out of the tree.
!/docs/patterns/
!/docs/patterns/**
!/docs/references/
!/docs/references/**
# Dated analysis notes. Same reason as the two above, one step earlier in the
# workflow: these are the written record of measurements this repo's agents cite
# when they decide what to build, and a measurement nobody can find again is a
# measurement that gets made twice.
!/docs/analysis/
!/docs/analysis/**
# The surfaces registry: which user surface, which content class, which layer is
# solved and on what evidence. It exists because an agent re-derived a six-day-old
# measurement from scratch; the answer to that is a findable record, not a better memory.
!/docs/surfaces/
!/docs/surfaces/**
# Lesson ledger: known errors, proven paths, edge cases. Kept in git so a lesson
# can be diffed across versions rather than living only in a session transcript.
!/docs/lessons/
!/docs/lessons/**
/.local/
/backlog

/.pi/todos
/.pi/issues
/.pi/cache
/result
/result-*

/.wrangler/
**/.wrangler/
.cartography/
.superpowers/

# Tool residue that is not work: playwright MCP output and wt.sh reconcile logs
.playwright-mcp/
.wt-rec-test.log
